title: "SpheroidalWaves.jl: Arbitrary-precision prolate and oblate spheroidal wave functions."
version: 0.7.0
identifiers:
- type: doi
  value: 10.5281/zenodo.19728039
- type: url
  value: https://brandynlucca.github.io/SpheroidalWaves.jl
abstract: SpheroidalWaves.jl is a Julia package for the numerical evaluation and analysis of 
  prolate and oblate spheroidal wave functions. It combines a Julia interface with shared 
  Fortran numerical kernels, supporting real and complex spheroidal parameters, complex evaluation 
  coordinates, and double, quadruple, and runtime-selectable arbitrary precision using MPFR and 
  MPC. The package computes angular and radial functions, characteristic values, expansion 
  coefficients, and connection and normalization quantities. Additional capabilities include 
  coordinate and parameter derivatives, combined evaluations, parameter sweeps, inverse eigenvalue 
  calculations, and searches for zeros and stationary points. Numerical diagnostics provide 
  accuracy estimates and consistency checks, while scaled representations and endpoint treatments 
  support calculations in challenging parameter regimes. Batch evaluation, thread-safe execution, 
  and reusable numerical workspaces support repeated computations. These capabilities provide a 
  consistent interface for incorporating spheroidal wave functions into scientific calculations 
  requiring flexible precision, sensitivity analysis, and numerical verification.
